  {:id :f2-unvalidated-consumed-revoke-clock :severity :confirmed-synthetic-input-gap
   :source "model:336-347,409-430; tests:259-274,466-511"
   :finding "The revoke event shape requires a clock key but does not validate its value. Once state is consumed or revoked, branches 422-423 return already-consumed/already-revoked before validating clock or updating last-clock. Thus an alist with clock nil is accepted as already-consumed, and a chronologically later revoke can be followed by an earlier final sample checked only against the earlier consume clock. This violates the planned malformed-clock denial and the synthetic ordered-clock model; it is not a claim of a real revocation bypass."
   :minimal-fix "Define and consistently apply closed revoke-clock validity and continuity for every revoke variant, including consumed/closed and already-revoked, without converting already-consumed into a consent ACK or canceling a valid pending final. On an invalid/uncertain sample fail closed and specify whether pending is closed; when a valid sample is accepted, update or otherwise preserve the time-order baseline before any subsequent final. Preserve terminal storage-unavailable behavior."
